From a4ccd6fec033a650c1b980015f9c624ea2ea1e7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zambia Treasury Insight <patch@local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:23:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] Tier 1 #4: Pre-2020 inflation backfill (CPI_YOY
 extended to 2004-01)

Replaces data/manual/CPI_YOY.csv (78 rows, 2020-02 -> 2026-10) with a 271-row
version (2004-01 -> 2026-10). The pre-2020 rows are derived from the Zambia CPI
1994=100 index level series in the BoZ 'Real Effective Exchange Rates' sheet,
computing YoY as (CPI_t / CPI_{t-12} - 1) * 100.

Cleaning steps applied to the source CPI level:
  - Outlier rows with |MoM change| > 30% dropped (catches the 110.7 typo at 2025-09
    that would have produced a -98% / +8000% YoY spike).
  - Snapped mid-month publication dates to month-end reference dates.
  - Reindexed to a complete monthly range; small gaps (<=2 months) interpolated.

The repo's authoritative ZamStats direct releases are kept unchanged for
2020-02 onward (78 rows). 193 new rows are appended for 2004-01 -> 2020-01.

Validation: pre-2020 range 5.2-22.8% YoY, consistent with known ZamStats prints
(2016 drought spike ~22.8%, 2012 low ~5.2%). 70 tests still pass.
